course: dictionary
lesson: 15543
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word «sup» is a good example. Look at the words around it first, then ask which meaning fits.
explain: «Grandma likes to sup her tea slowly by the fire.» Here sup means to drink a little at a time, or to sip. The clue is slowly: you cannot sup something quickly and in a rush.
explain: «The family sat down to sup together at seven o'clock.» Now sup means to eat supper, the evening meal. The clues are the time and the word together. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: «Grandad took a sup of water and smiled.» Here sup is a noun: a small mouthful of a drink. The word «a» in front is a clue, because you can say a sup just as you can say a bite. Young people text it differently again: «Hey Sam, sup?» is a short way of saying «What's up?»
fact: Sup is a verb, a noun and a slang greeting, so it has several meanings.
fact: «Sup» means to sip a drink, a little at a time.
fact: «Sup» can also mean to eat supper, the evening meal.
fact: A «sup» is a small mouthful of a drink.
fact: «'Sup?» (slang) means «What's up?», a friendly way of saying hi and asking how someone is.
exercise: «Grandma likes to sup her tea slowly by the fire.» What does sup mean here? | *To sip a drink a little at a time | To cook a meal | To sing a loud song | To run very fast
exercise: «The family sat down to sup together at seven o'clock.» What does sup mean here? | To clean the table | To go for a long walk | To go to sleep early | *To eat the evening meal
exercise: «Grandad took a sup of water and smiled.» In this sentence, what is a sup? | A large plate of food | *A small mouthful of a drink | A tall glass | A type of bread
test: Ben texts his friend, «Sup?» What does he mean? | Do you want some soup for lunch? | *A short way of saying hi and asking how you are | A loud shout for help | A grey, wet day
test: «Mum asked us to sup our milk slowly.» What does sup mean? | To spill it on the floor | To dance around the kitchen | To throw the cup away | *To sip, drinking slowly
exam: What does sup mean in «The guests gathered to sup, and the cook served a hot stew.»? | To pack their bags and leave | To shout loudly across the room | *To eat supper, the evening meal | To take one drop of water
